From 3c20def968ed6690c862b811f2b276e32fb6643e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Valery Petrov <valerypetrov@icloud.com>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 03:12:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Pin a shard that is this server itself to the in-process path

The shard-target check and the pre-check of the local shard's grants
both assume a shard that is this server itself is read and written in
process, on the caller's context: that is where an undeclared database
resolves to the caller's current one. SelectStreamFactory and the sink
take that path only with prefer_localhost_replica on and, for a read,
task-based parallel replicas off; a caller setting them the other way
had the probe validate one table while the shard read another, and the
grant pre-check ask for grants the connection path never needs.

Pin both on the context that executes the generated read, on the query
endpoints and the table functions alike, and prefer_localhost_replica on
the write's context next to the delivery settings it already pins, so
the three places agree whatever the caller brings. The probe treats a
local replica as this context unconditionally. The tests read a wrapper
over a one-replica and a two-replica local shard with
prefer_localhost_replica off and with parallel replicas on, and expect
the caller's own database either way, with the grant refusal still first.

